_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.12303867893817881,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.12448,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":83.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Figure Technology Solutions, Inc., a financial technology company, provides blockchain-based products and solutions in the United States. The company offers a suite of blockchain-based solutions for its marketplaces, including lending, trading, and investing activities in areas, such as consumer credit and digital assets. It also provides technology-enabled loan origination system and pairs this system with a distribution marketplace; Figure Connect that provides access to a deep and broad pool of capital markets partners; and develops an exchange for digital assets and credit, which offers interest-bearing stablecoin deposits. The company was formerly known as FT Intermediate, Inc. and changed its name to Figure Technology Solutions, Inc. in August 2025. Figure Technology Solutions, Inc. was founded in 2018 and is based in Reno, Nevada.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael Benjamin Tannenbaum | CEO & Director | Age 36 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 602 people. Revenue per employee of $842K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $70K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $104K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Figure Technology Solutions, In is a mid-cap financial services business with a $6.0B market cap on $507M of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 45% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 35-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $42M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders. Cash conversion is thin at 0.47\u00d7, however, which raises the oldest question in analysis: are these earnings backed by cash?.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 2.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 12% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 12% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 320% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":3.1952072145596073},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.2M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2162385.85},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Among the least levered in Financial Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Wall Street Analysts Believe Figure Technology (FIGR) Could Rally 77.48%: Here's is How to Trade","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3032493/wall-street-analysts-believe-figure-technology-figr-could-rally-77-48-here-s-is-how-to-trade?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cconsensus_price_target-3032493","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795096503.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Figure Technology Solutions (NASDAQ:FIGR) Shares Up 3.8% \u2013 Time to Buy?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/17/figure-technology-solutions-nasdaqfigr-shares-up-3-8-time-to-buy.html","date":"2026-11-17","timestamp":1794942299.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.883,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Figure Technology Solutions (FIGR) Could Be 46% Undervalued After New Credit Facility And Q3 Profit","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nasdaq-figr/figure-technology-solutions/news/figure-technology-solutions-figr-could-be-46-undervalued-aft","date":"2026-11-17","timestamp":1794914266.527,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.969,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Figure Technology Solutions (NASDAQ:FIGR) Stock Price Target Cut by Mizuho","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/16/figure-technology-solutions-nasdaqfigr-stock-price-target-cut-by-mizuho.html","date":"2026-11-16","